==Trivia==
*In the same way that [[The Edge of Spacetime]] through [[Garden of Wilted Thoughts]] take place in an altered, mirrored Japan, the map used in Stratospheric Pathway through [[Truth's Devouring Maw]] is North and South America but jumbled up and rearranged.
*Each stage is a different reference to American culture:
**[[Permission to Land]]'s Japanese name, Jiyū e no Jōriku-chi (自由への上陸地, "Landing Point to Freedom"), mentions freedom and may specifically reference "Land of the Free", a phrase in "[[wikipedia:The Star-Spangled Banner|The Star-Spangled Banner]]" commonly used as a nickname for the U.S. The stage also has an eagle on its [[Media:Rc017.png|enemy base]].
**[[Steps Great and Small]] is similar to "That's one small step for [a] man, one giant leap for mankind," a famous quote by American astronaut [[wikipedia:Neil Armstrong|Neil Armstrong]]. The reference is more apparent in its Japanese name, Ōinaru Chīsaki Ippo (大いなる小さき一歩, "One Great Little Step").
**[[Burger Garden]] mentions burgers, which have been an iconic food of the United States for [[wikipedia:History of the hamburger in the United States|many years]].
**[[Small Inlet, Large Field]]'s Japanese name, Ōkusabara no Chīsana Irie (大草原の小さな入り江, "Little Inlet on the Prairie"), references ''[[wikipedia:Little House on the Prairie|Little House on the Prairie]]'', an American children's novel series that inspired a [[wikipedia:Little House on the Prairie (TV series)|live-action TV series]] and an [[wikipedia:Laura, the Prairie Girl|anime]].
**[[Bubbly Dream]]'s Japanese name, Baburī-kan Dorīmu (バブリー感ドリーム, "Bubbly-feeling Dream"), sounds similar to ''Amerikan Dorīmu'' (アメリカンドリーム, [[wikipedia:American Dream|American Dream]]).
**[[Prairie Harbor]]'s Japanese name, Gurēto Purērī Minato (グレートプレーリー港, "Great Prairie Harbor"), may reference the [[wikipedia:Great Plains|Great Plains region]] or [[wikipedia:Grand Prairie, Texas|Grand Prairie]], a city in Texas.
**The [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]] in Burger Garden, Small Inlet, Large Field and Bubbly Dream may allude to the stars on the U.S. flag.
*Stratospheric Pathway is the first [[Zero Legends]] sub-chapter not to reintroduce a former event-exclusive enemy.

